# =============================================================================
# CeolX — Environment Variables Overview
# =============================================================================
# Variables are split per app. See each app's own .env.example for details:
#
#   apps/server/.env.example   — backend secrets (DB, auth, OAuth, Stripe, etc.)
#   apps/native/.env.example   — Expo public vars (EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix)
#   apps/web/.env.example      — Vite client vars (VITE_ prefix) + build-time vars
#
# =============================================================================
# envx-cli workflow (https://www.npmjs.com/package/envx-cli)
# =============================================================================
#
# First-time setup:
#   npm install -g envx-cli
#   cp .envrc.example .envrc
#   # Edit .envrc — set DEVELOPMENT_SECRET, STAGING_SECRET, PRODUCTION_SECRET
#   source .envrc
#
# Daily dev (decrypt → .env in each app dir):
#   envx copy -e development
#
# After editing .env.development files (re-encrypt before committing):
#   envx encrypt -e development -s DEVELOPMENT_SECRET
#   git add apps/server/.env.development.gpg apps/native/.env.development.gpg apps/web/.env.development.gpg
#
# Onboarding a new developer:
#   1. Share DEVELOPMENT_SECRET securely (1Password / Bitwarden)
#   2. They run: cp .envrc.example .envrc && echo 'export DEVELOPMENT_SECRET="..."' >> .envrc
#   3. source .envrc && envx copy -e development
#
# Environment ↔ Git branch ↔ Neon DB branch mapping:
#   development → local Docker PostgreSQL
#   staging     → Neon staging branch  → git staging branch
#   production  → Neon main branch     → git main branch
# =============================================================================
